    "description": "Profiles of {n} countries and territories with flag, capital, population, GDP, currency, calling code and time zones: World Bank figures with world ranks.",
    "h1": "Countries of the world: flags, capitals and population",
    "lede": "Every country and territory with World Bank figures, by continent: flag, capital and population. Open one for its GDP, currency, calling code, time zones and about 50 more figures, each with its world rank.",
    "about": [
      "Figures come from the World Bank World Development Indicators, the same snapshot as the data tables on this site, so a rank on a profile matches the rank in the table it links to. Capitals come from Wikidata and flags from the flag-icons project.",
      "Names follow the Unicode list your browser uses for your language. The list covers every economy the World Bank reports on, including some territories, so it is not a list of United Nations members."
    ],
    "faq": [
      {
        "q": "How many countries are on this list?",
        "a": "{n} countries and territories: every economy the World Bank reports figures for. Some, such as Hong Kong, Puerto Rico or Greenland, are territories rather than independent countries."
      },
      {
        "q": "Where do the capitals and flags come from?",
        "a": "Capitals are the ones Wikidata lists for each place (CC0). Where a capital is disputed, no capital is shown. Flags are SVG images from the flag-icons project (MIT licence)."
      },
      {
        "q": "How current are the numbers?",
        "a": "Each profile shows the year of every figure and the date of the snapshot. The World Bank publishes most figures a year or two after the fact, so some values are older than others."
      }
    ],
